    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47084" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sur-rustĭcus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subr-</span></b> ), a, um,
			adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>somewhat clownish</i> or <i>rustic</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sonare subagreste quiddam planeque surrusticum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Brut. 74, 259</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Or. 48, 161</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pudor quidam paene surrusticus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Fam. 5, 12, 1</span></i>
			.— * <i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">surrustĭcē</span></b> ,
				<i>somewhat clownishly</i>, Gell. praef.
			§ 10.</div>
